{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02WX", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-algebraic-space}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b2d9eabd8c87b0e238cbea1b94302144c326bbf4c48fdd8c7029c6f7c91934f3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe start building our arsenal of lemmas dealing with algebraic spaces.\nThe first result says that in Definition <REF_0001>\nwe can weaken the condition on the diagonal as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:28e3ab70c6a778612123878484b45c4db18c4c2939b411e3fcfef0b18a1b84ed", "unit_id": "tag:02WX:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02WX", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$F$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\in \\Ob((\\Sch/S)_{fppf})$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to F$", "MATH_0007": "$F$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-locally-representable-gives-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:196ad52b113253433e1521114ebd90f48e6511a224fc027a8761896aec4ccc60", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3b0e686931716869382c794b9d0d0090a9d13e103e8d9c2e662870bbc9142b2c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a sheaf on <MATH_0004>\nsuch that there exists <MATH_0005> and a map\n<MATH_0006> which is representable, surjective, and <ACCENT_0001>tale.\nThen <MATH_0007> is an algebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:61e027d3b2819aba4baae64640fdacc46e4a9fe01dccf2d8901f1267f18015ea", "unit_id": "tag:0BGQ:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02WX", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$R = U \\times_F U$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to F$", "MATH_0003": "$s, t : R \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to F$", "MATH_0005": "$j = (t, s) : R \\to U \\times_S U$", "MATH_0006": "$R = U \\times_F U$", "MATH_0007": "$F' = U/R$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to F'$", "MATH_0009": "$R = U \\times_F U$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to F' \\to F$", "MATH_0011": "$F' \\to F$", "MATH_0012": "$U \\to F$", "MATH_0013": "$F' \\to F$", "MATH_0014": "$F' = F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-surjective-flat-locally-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e44eaa7a9623f1d2185f35de4f0d7fdd109ff3d33eaef37b5972f112413dcef8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:84ea89b3532055ac0e810ae3d4112922623d679a1e3d3bd5a1d9fd66c2d4b9dd", "source_text": "Set <MATH_0001>. This is a scheme as <MATH_0002> is assumed representable.\nThe projections <MATH_0003> are <ACCENT_0001>tale as <MATH_0004> is assumed <ACCENT_0002>tale.\nThe map <MATH_0005> is a monomorphism and an equivalence\nrelation as <MATH_0006>. By Theorem <REF_0001>\nthe quotient sheaf <MATH_0007> is an algebraic space and <MATH_0008>\nis surjective and <ACCENT_0003>tale. Again since <MATH_0009> we obtain\na canonical factorization <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> is an injective\nmap of sheaves. On the other hand, <MATH_0012> is surjective as a map\nof sheaves by Lemma <REF_0002>.\nThus <MATH_0013> is also surjective and we conclude <MATH_0014> is an\nalgebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e260f11af7e1846476e83e5d2759e82aa7a61d4ce052e7fe469c050816bd9a25", "unit_id": "tag:0BGQ:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02WX", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$G$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$F$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0007": "$G \\to F$", "MATH_0008": "$F$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-locally-representable-by-space-gives-space}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1e5cc94bfd2078725082590d7a9b9043344df27c28b11c65f549925c2a35316e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c80c0dd0df0057810e85b42e1905620eae62bbd6cbc24950776af0f6bb990114", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003> be an algebraic\nspace over <MATH_0004>, let <MATH_0005> be a sheaf on <MATH_0006>, and let\n<MATH_0007> be a representable transformation of functors which is\nsurjective and <ACCENT_0001>tale. Then <MATH_0008> is an algebraic space.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:206098f7158d1a067aa12ead5decd04d5848400bbbd876165662fab5d599fd9d", "unit_id": "tag:0BGR:statement"}
